---
import TrainingLayout from "../../layouts/TrainingLayout.astro";
import Snippet from "../../components/training/Snippet.astro";
import LiveDemo from "../../components/training/LiveDemo.astro";
import ApiLink from "../../components/training/ApiLink.astro";
import ChapterLink from "../../components/training/ChapterLink.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/training/Callout.astro";
import NineAreas from "../../components/training/diagrams/NineAreas.astro";
---
<TrainingLayout slug="fixed-columns">

  <h2 id="model">Fixed columns belong to the model</h2>
  <p>
    Two numbers in <ApiLink name="TableFactory.createTableModel" />: <code>fixedLeftColumnCount</code> and
    <code>fixedRightColumnCount</code>. The first <em>n</em> columns go to the <strong>west</strong> side, the last <em>m</em>
    to the <strong>east</strong> side – in header, body and footer.
  </p>
  <NineAreas />
  <Snippet file="demos/fixed-columns.ts" region="model" title="src/model/order-wide-model.ts" />
  <p>The 30 month columns are generated – 40 columns in total:</p>
  <Snippet file="demos/fixed-columns.ts" region="wide" />
  <LiveDemo name="fixed-columns" title="40 columns, ID and Total fixed" height={400}
            caption="Scroll sideways: ID stays on the left, Total on the right – in the footer, too." />

  <h2 id="horizontal">Horizontal virtual scrolling</h2>
  <p>
    Look at the DOM count in the toolbar: of 40 columns only the visible ones are rendered. The table virtualises in
    both directions – that's why a table with 400 columns is as fast as one with 10.
  </p>

  <Callout type="pitfall" title="Not in the options">
    <p>There is no <code>fixedLeftColumnCount</code> in <ApiLink name="TableOptions" />. It's part of the model:
      <ApiLink name="TableModelIf.getFixedLeftColumnCount" /> and <ApiLink name="TableModelIf.getFixedRightColumnCount" />.</p>
  </Callout>
  <Callout type="tip" title="Footer by property">
    <p>The totals footer of <ChapterLink slug="footer-totals" /> finds its columns by property – it works unchanged although
      “Total” moved from position 10 to position 40.</p>
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="row-numbers">Row numbers – a fixed column for free</h2>
  <p>
    The most common fixed column is the row number of a spreadsheet. One flag in
    <ApiLink name="TableFactory.createTableModel" /> puts a <ApiLink name="RowNumberColumnDef" /> in front of your columns and
    fixes it on the left – <code>fixedLeftColumnCount</code> counts it automatically:
  </p>
  <Snippet file="demos/row-numbers.ts" region="model" />
  <ul>
    <li>The width follows the largest number – <code>9</code>, <code>100,000</code> or <code>2,000,000</code>; filter to a few
      rows and the column gets narrower again.</li>
    <li><code>mode: "display"</code> (default) numbers the view 1, 2, 3 … – also after sorting and filtering.
      <code>mode: "original"</code> keeps the number with its row. <ApiLink name="RowNumberOptionsIf" /> has the rest:
      <code>format</code>, <code>headerLabel</code>, <code>exported</code>, <code>minWidthInPx</code>.</li>
    <li>With selection type <code>"range"</code> a click on a number selects the whole row, Shift-click a block of rows,
      Ctrl/⌘-click toggles one; a click on <code>#</code> selects all.</li>
  </ul>
  <Snippet file="demos/row-numbers.ts" region="selection" />
  <LiveDemo name="row-numbers" title="100,000 orders with row numbers" height={360}
            caption="Click a number, Shift-click another. Sort by total, then switch to original numbers – they stay with their rows." />
  <Callout type="pitfall" title="Every other column index is one higher">
    <p>The row numbers are a real column (like a <ApiLink name="CheckboxColumnDef" />): with the flag, “Total” is column 11,
      not 10 – in events, <code>getValueAt</code> and <code>scrollToIndex</code>. Ask by property:
      <ApiLink name="TableApi.getColumnIndex" />. With your own area models put the column definition in yourself – first,
      counted in <code>fixedLeftColumnCount</code>; a checkbox column comes after it.</p>
  </Callout>
  <Callout type="version">
    <p>Since 1.1.93. Not in copy and Excel export unless <code>exported: true</code>; screen readers hear the numbers as row
      headers.</p>
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="next">Next</h2>
  <p>Part 5 starts with the options: <ChapterLink slug="table-options" />.</p>
</TrainingLayout>
